"title":"","content":"I've considered it further and I'm willing to give this a shot, but I can't promise how often I'll be able to participate... I'll most likely play a drifting Nuwisha that plays both sides to his advantage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4148-feroke","name":"FeroKE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T06:14:14-07:00","id":290466,"title":"","content":"Awesome! I have at least one player!<br /> <br /> Don't worry to much about &quot;showing up&quot; a whole lot. My picture of how the game ran is that I make a post, then I check my email a few times a day to see if y'all made a post, then I'll reply, and so on. PbP are slower (so our combats will be truncated to save time, if you don't mind). We might try limiting posting about combat to ones that matter (If your going to kill the one Bane that you managed to surprise that guarding the hidden puzzle, then I say &quot;tell me how you kill the little freak&quot;). Perhaps, even for the combats that matter a little bit (one where there is a chance of something dramatic happening if you lose, like PC death or vital NPC death or something), we will limit combat to 3-5 posts per player, and then we will just choreograph the rest (so you get a chance to use your gifts you work hard to buy, or neat tactics that you want to try).<br /> <br /> Count on their being tons of dialogue and more tons of investigation, especially since your &quot;Gaia's Teacher&quot;...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Litera scripta manet&quot;<br /> Check out my blog at <a href=\"http://www.murkypool.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.murkypool.blogspot.com</a><br /> <br /> Hire me! Copywriting, Adobe InDesign work, Grant Writing, Social Media Managment, RPG writing and more! Contact at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#422f23362a36302d2c2b3a02252f232b2e6c212d2f\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"c0ada1b4a8b4b2afaea9b880a7ada1a9aceea3afad\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3381-murky-master","name":"Murky Master","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3381_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T21:22:23-07:00","id":290999,"title":"","content":"It's cool, I'll do a write up for the character and e-mail it to you when I get the chance... should be able to knock it out some time this weekend<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4148-feroke","name":"FeroKE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T04:59:05-07:00","id":291198,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Now don't be shy forums crawlers, y'all can join in too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Litera scripta manet&quot;<br /> Check out my blog at <a href=\"http://www.murkypool.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.murkypool.blogspot.com</a><br /> <br /> Hire me! Copywriting, Adobe InDesign work, Grant Writing, Social Media Managment, RPG writing and more! Contact at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#573a36233f232538393e2f17303a363e3b7934383a\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"1a777b6e726e68757473625a7d777b737634797577\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3381-murky-master","name":"Murky Master","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3381_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T11:30:39-07:00","id":291464,"title":"","content":"I'll join. I've got some vampire concepts kicking around I wouldn't mind trying out.<br /> <br /> Just got some questions to ask first.<br /> <br /> -Are there any restrictions Clans and Sects?<br /> -Have any of the big metaplot events happened, like the Week of Nightmares, or are we keeping things like x20 Ed, the metaplot rewound back to just before those events started?<br /> -When it comes to character creation I assume we're using the default amounts from the rulebooks, creating young vampires/werewolves and not older, more potent ones.<br /> -Which Edition we're using is kind of important as they've some notable tweaks between Rev Ed and x20 Ed. For instance the Dodge Talent has been rolled into Athletics, Linguistics is now a Merit, etc. So yeah... are we using Rev Ed then since you don't have the x20 books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:05:37-07:00","id":291525,"title":"","content":"AkatsukiLeader13<br /> <br /> 1. No clan, sect, or bloodline restrictions<br /> 2. Have whatever metaplot events in your background that you like, but I don't anticiate I will be using any future events. The PCs might THINK Gehenna is coming...<br /> 3. We have one Nuwisha werewolf and an 8th gen True Brujah so far, so I suppose a new vampire would be fine.<br /> 4. Its gonna have to Rev edition, but I kind of like that dodge is rolled into Athletics. I might house rule some stuff in that sounds neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Litera scripta manet&quot;<br /> Check out my blog at <a href=\"http://www.murkypool.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.murkypool.blogspot.com</a><br /> <br /> Hire me! Copywriting, Adobe InDesign work, Grant Writing, Social Media Managment, RPG writing and more! Contact at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#2e434f5a465a5c414047566e49434f4742004d4143\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"90fdf1e4f8e4e2fffef9e8d0f7fdf1f9fcbef3fffd\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3381-murky-master","name":"Murky Master","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3381_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:35:28-07:00","id":291577,"title":"","content":"Well recently Embraced 8th Generation vampire is possible. Maxing out the the normal Generation Background will put you at that level. But what I meant was that we don't start off with XP or extra freeibe points, Character Creation uses the defaults presented in the Rulebooks.<br /> <br /> But that is a shame that you don't have the x20 Ed books. As good as the Rev Ed was, x20 Ed is much, much better. They tweaked and fine-tuned plenty of the issues Rev Ed had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T05:12:22-07:00","id":291959,"title":"","content":"I understand. Yes we will start of with the 15 freebie points that revised says you get.<br /> <br /> I do wish I had those books, but I'm not exactly rolling in money right now. That's the only reason I don't have the thing in my hands right now. Otherwise I would not mind deferring to whatever differences are in the v20 book.<br /> <br /> Besides, the art looked awesome on the kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Litera scripta manet&quot;<br /> Check out my blog at <a href=\"http://www.murkypool.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.murkypool.blogspot.com</a><br /> <br /> Hire me! Copywriting, Adobe InDesign work, Grant Writing, Social Media Managment, RPG writing and more!